0..79 Comment "/// This source states the Hopf family over the 2-sphere. Its arm at the 2-cell"
80..106 Comment "/// is `ua` of a homotopy."
107..110 Comment "///"
111..189 Comment "/// `ua` takes an n-cell of `P ≃ P` at each dimension. At dimension two, the"
190..269 Comment "/// cell is a homotopy of the identity of `P`. Such a map sends each point to a"
270..304 Comment "/// path from the point to itself."
305..308 Comment "///"
309..385 Comment "/// The checker reads the cell by its type. `ua` of the identity equivalence"
386..464 Comment "/// converts to reflexivity at the type. Transport of a point `y` along `ua h`"
465..544 Comment "/// is `h y`, in the checker and in the kernel. `Path.ap` of the Hopf family on"
545..620 Comment "/// the 2-cell reduces to its arm, `ua selfloop`. Transport of `Base` along"
621..645 Comment "/// that cell is `loop`."
646..649 Comment "///"
650..725 Comment "/// Limits: the image of a cell into the universe is the whole image of one"
726..803 Comment "/// letter along one call. A word of more letters, or an inverse letter, does"
804..819 Comment "/// not reduce."
820..823 Comment "///"
824..874 Comment "/// - see: #6530 — the universe family at a cell"
875..925 Comment "/// - see: #6458 — `Path.ap` of a case on a cell"
926..997 Comment "/// - see: #6477 — `ua` of the identity equivalence is the empty word"
998..1078 Comment "/// - see: #6282 — transport along a longer word in a family into the universe"
1079..1129 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere-maps.gandr"
1130..1179 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/univalence.gandr"
1181..1197 Comment "// The 2-sphere."
